                "caption": "Figure 5:Register attention dynamics in one attention head.We visualize LLaDA layer 29, head 13 during prompt-visible carryover generation. The left panel shows the clean previous chunk, while the three right panels show the next chunk at successive denoising stages after the context reset. When the previous chunk is fully denoised, this attention head plays a write-heavy role: register queries attend to output keys (top inset), while output-to-register reads are weak. After the next chunk is re-noised, the head switches into a read-heavy role: output queries attend strongly to register keys (lower insets) throughout denoising.",
